\zlabel{triptych:concise:overview:start}
\begin{sensestable}
\zlabel{triptych:concise:sense:literal}Literal & Distinct voices confess justice, seek mercy, command love, intercede and undertake fidelity. The three prayers ask God to sustain the life the readings require.\\
\zlabel{triptych:concise:sense:allegorical}Allegorical & David's Son is Lord; Word and Spirit establish the people whom Christ gathers, speaks with as Head, and nourishes through his mysteries.\\
\zlabel{triptych:concise:sense:moral}Moral & Grace forms an undivided heart, patient common life and fulfilled commitments. Love seeks the neighbor's good through truthful mercy and fitting correction.\\
\zlabel{triptych:concise:sense:anagogical}Anagogical & One hope, the Lord's judgment and the eternal remedy direct present healing toward perfected charity and communion with God and the saints.\\
\end{sensestable}
\zlabel{triptych:concise:overview:end}
\clearpage
